Cyde Weys wrote:

> What is "death drop"?  Is that when you kill a monster carrying items and 
> get them?

There are three kinds of items that are dropped to the ground when a 
monster dies:

1. Monsters inventory
2. Special items that are generated from the monsters body: dragon 
scales, unicon horns, worm tooths, quarterstaffs, Q's box, etc.
3. Random items.

The third group is usually called 'the death drop'. It's existence is 
controversial issue. IIRC it is the only way that random items are 
generated in the game after all levels are generated.

I've ratinalized it by saying that it's those items that the monsterd 
had but had forgotten having. The same items you notice that you had but 
didn't remember to use when you died. It could be even coded so that 
they are generated in the monsters inventory (so that a probe would show 
them) but are unusable for the monster.

